{"name":"Burgundy","hex":"#900020","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Burgundy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A historical region and former administrative region of France; since 2016, part of the administrative region of Bourgogne-Franche-Comté.","An early-medieval kingdom and later former duchy in France and the Netherlands."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A variety of wine from this region, chiefly red wine made with pinot noir grapes.","A variety of wine resembling that of Burgundy; especially from Australia or California."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Burgundy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Burgundy","blocks":[{"text":"Burgundy is a historical region in France, broadly corresponding to the territory of the former administrative region of the same name, which existed from 1982 to 2015 before it was merged on 1 January 2016 into Bourgogne-Franche-Comté. Its capital is Dijon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Flag_of_Bourgogne.svg/330px-Flag_of_Bourgogne.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burgundy","wikidata":"Q1173"},{"title":"Burgundy (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Burgundy is a purplish, dark-red color. The name comes from the Burgundy wine in France. The word \"burgundy\" is not usually capitalized."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Danish_Passport_Cover.svg/330px-Danish_Passport_Cover.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burgundy_(color)","wikidata":"Q797446"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Chatillon-sur-Seine_-_Mus%C3%A9e_du_Pays_chatillonnais_-_Crat%C3%A8re_de_Vix_-_012_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Chatillon-sur-Seine_-_Mus%C3%A9e_du_Pays_chatillonnais_-_Crat%C3%A8re_de_Vix_-_012_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaig